SUMMARY:Deadline: Go Short 2027: International Short Film Festival Nijmegen
  Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Go Short\, the international short film festival in Nijmegen\, 
 is open for entries for its 19th edition (6 to 11 April 2027). A small\, a
 pproachable Dutch festival that programmes fiction\, documentary\, animati
 on and experimental shorts.\n\nOrganisation: Go Short\, International Shor
 t Film Festival Nijmegen\nLocation: Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Compe
 tition open to films made in Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Ar
 rivals Competition for European film school projects.\nAward: Small submis
 sion fees per tier: EUR 12.50 (early bird\, 15 September 2026)\, EUR 15 (r
 egular\, 15 November) or EUR 20 (late\, 15 December) for films\; EUR 8/10/
 12 for video games\, VR/XR\, performances and installations\; EUR 7.50 fla
 t for music videos. Awards include the Go Short Award for Best European Sh
 ort\, Best Dutch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award (amo
 unts not published in the call).\nDuration: Festival 6 to 11 April 2027\n\
 nMore: https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-202
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open to films made in
  Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Competition for Europ
 ean film school projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T132211Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops).\n\nOrganisation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)
 \nLocation: Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are in
 vited to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a c
 ontribution to travel costs.\nAward: All films in the International Select
 ion are equal winners of the EMAF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screenin
 g fees: EUR 250 for Features\, EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending
  on length\, EUR 500 for installations and expanded projects\; production 
 costs for installations and expanded projects are paid by the festival. Se
 lected artists get free accreditation\, three hotel nights (longer if setu
 p requires) and a travel cost contribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festi
 val in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027\; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 
 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
